<article class="env-remark" id="0FMZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FMZ">Remark <span data-tag="0FMZ">50.15.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $Y \subset X$ be an effective Cartier divisor. If the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge \longrightarrow \mathcal{O}_{Y, y}^\wedge  \]
</div>
  <p> has a section for all $y \in Y$, then the de Rham complex of log poles is defined for $Y \subset X$ over $S$. If we ever need this result we will formulate a precise statement and add a proof here. </p>
</article>